DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssddppccoonnttrrooll utility attempts to query the specified Service Discovery
     Protocol (SDP) server.  Remote SDP servers are identified by their ad‐
     dress.  Connection to the local SDP server is made via the control
     socket.  The ssddppccoonnttrrooll utility uses Service Search Attribute Requests
     and prints results to standard output and error messages to standard er‐
     ror.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa _a_d_d_r_e_s_s
             Connect to the remote device with the specified address.  The ad‐
             dress can be specified as BD_ADDR or a name.  If a name was spec‐
             ified, the ssddppccoonnttrrooll utility attempts to resolve the name via
             bt_gethostbyname(3).

     --cc _p_a_t_h
             Specify path to the control socket.  The default path is
             _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_s_d_p.

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

     --ll      Query the local SDP server via the control socket.

     _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
             One of the supported commands (see below).  The special command
             hheellpp can be used to obtain a list of all supported commands.  To
             get more information about a specific command, use hheellpp _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.

     _p_a_r_a_m_e_t_e_r_s
             One or more optional space separated command parameters.

